{"raw": {"https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=537246337": {"title": "Head Track and Cross-Country Coach", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Head Track and Cross-Country Coach Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type FTS Required Degree 4 Year Degree Manage Others Yes Description The Head Track and Cross-Country Coach provides Christ-centered leadership for Crown College's NCAA Division III Track and Cross-Country programs The coach is responsible for developing student-athletes spiritually, academically, personally, and athletically while advancing the mission of Crown College. The position oversees all aspects of the programs, including recruiting, coaching, administration, compliance, staff leadership, and community engagement. Supervisor: This position reports to the Vice President of Athletics Essential Functions: \u00b7 Provide vision, leadership, and oversight for all aspects of the NCAA Division III Track and Field and Cross Country programs. \u00b7 Lead year-round recruiting efforts. \u00b7 Build and maintain a roster of academically, athletically, and spiritually qualified student-athletes. \u00b7 Plan and oversee practices, player development, game preparation, and competition. \u00b7 Ensure NCAA, conference, and institutional compliance. \u00b7 Disciple and mentor student-athletes spiritually, academically, athletically, and personally. \u00b7 Monitor academic progress and support student success. \u00b7 Complete administrative responsibilities accurately and on time. \u00b7 Manage budgets, scheduling, travel, equipment, camps, and fundraising. Physical Demands The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to perform the essential functions of this position successfully. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. \u00b7 Sit or stand for extended periods and perform extensive computer and mobile-device work. \u00b7 Possess hand and arm dexterity, or an equivalent ability, sufficient for keyboard use and operation of creative-production equipment. \u00b7 Communicate effectively with coworkers, students, partners, and constituents by telephone, video conference, and in person. \u00b7 Possess adequate vision to accommodate frequent viewing of computer screens and review of visual content. \u00b7 Frequently lift or move up to 10 pounds and infrequently lift or move up to 25 pounds, including production equipment. \u00b7 Occasionally move throughout campus and off-campus locations and work in moderate-to-high noise environments during events. Qualifications: \u00b7 Demonstrated commitment to Jesus Christ and the mission of Crown College. \u00b7 Previous collegiate coaching and recruiting success. \u00b7 Knowledge of NCAA Division III rules and compliance. \u00b7 Bachelor's degree required; master's degree preferred. \u00b7 Agreement with and commitment to abide by the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant. Benefits: Crown College offers a generous and co prehensive benefits package for full-time staff and faculty, designed to support the health, well-being, and financial future of our employees. Benefits include medical coverage through Medica, dental coverage through Delta Dental, and vision coverage through EyeMed. Employees also receive employer-paid basic life insurance equal to one times their annual salary, subject to policy limits, with optional voluntary benefits including supplemental life insurance, hospital indemnity, critical illness, and short-term disability coverage. A Health Savings Account (HSA) is available for employees enrolled in the high-deductible health plan. In addition to competitive benefits, Crown offers generous paid vacation, sick leave, and holiday pay, along with a 403(b) retirement plan that includes an employer contribution. Environment and Location: Employees enjoy working on our beautiful lakeside campus, which features an on-campus fitness center, scenic walking paths leading to Parley Lake and convenient access to our on-campus Frisbie Golf Course. These amenities provide excellent opportunities to stay active, recharge, and enjoy the natural beauty of the campus throughout the year. Non-Discrimination Policy: Crown College provides equal employment opportunities to employees and applicants for employment without regard to sex, race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, familial status, status with regard to public assistance, genetic information, veteran status, or other applicable protected class status. As a private Christian college and religious educational institution, Crown College maintains the right to make employment decisions consistent with its religious beliefs, mission, Statement of Faith and Community Covenant, as permitted by applicable federal and state law."}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=537246336": {"title": "Assistant Baseball Coach", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Assistant Baseball Coach Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Coach - Stipend Description The Assistant Baseball Coach provides Christ-centered support for Crown College's NCAA Division III Baseball program. The coach is responsible for developing student-athletes spiritually, academically, personally, and athletically while advancing the mission of Crown College. The position assists and supports all aspects of the programs, including recruiting, coaching, administration, compliance, staff leadership, and community engagement and will primarily focus on hitting and infield play. Supervisor: This position reports to the Head Baseball Coach Essential Functions: \u00b7 Disciple and mentor student-athletes spiritually, academically, athletically, and personally. \u00b7 Monitor academic progress and support student success. \u00b7 Complete administrative responsibilities accurately and on time. \u00b7 Serve as the program\u2019s Hitting Coach and Infield Coach Coach first base during games Assist with offensive and defensive player development Assist with opponent scouting and game preparation Recruit prospective student-athletes in accordance with NCAA and institutional guidelines Assist with team travel arrangements and logistics Assist with administrative responsibilities associated with the baseball program Participate in practices, games, team activities, and other program responsibilities Support the overall mission, culture, and values of Crown College and the baseball program Physical Demands The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to perform the essential functions of this position successfully. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. \u00b7 Sit or stand for extended periods and perform extensive computer and mobile-device work. \u00b7 Possess hand and arm dexterity, or an equivalent ability, sufficient for keyboard use and operation of creative-production equipment. \u00b7 Communicate effectively with coworkers, students, partners, and constituents by telephone, video conference, and in person. \u00b7 Possess adequate vision to accommodate frequent viewing of computer screens and review of visual content. \u00b7 Frequently lift or move up to 10 pounds and infrequently lift or move up to 25 pounds, including production equipment. \u00b7 Occasionally move throughout campus and off-campus locations and work in moderate-to-high noise environments during events. Qualifications: \u00b7 Demonstrated commitment to Jesus Christ and the mission of Crown College. \u00b7 Previous collegiate coaching and recruiting success. \u00b7 Knowledge of NCAA Division III rules and compliance. \u00b7 Bachelor's degree required; master's degree preferred. \u00b7 Agreement with and commitment to abide by the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant. Non-discrimination Policy: Crown College provides equal employment opportunities to employees and applicants for employment without regard to sex, race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, familial status, status with regard to public assistance, genetic information, veteran status, or other applicable protected class status. As a private Christian college and religious educational institution, Crown College maintains the right to make employment decisions consistent with its religious beliefs, mission, Statement of Faith and Community Covenant, as permitted by applicable federal and state law. Additional Information Base Pay From 25,000"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=537225997": {"title": "Director of Creative Marketing", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Director of Creative Marketing Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type FTS Required Degree 4 Year Degree Manage Others Yes Minimum Experience 5 Years Contact information Name Fawn McCracken Email mccrackenf@crown.edu Description The Director of Creative Marketing provides strategic and hands-on leadership for Crown College\u2019s creative marketing, organic social media, multimedia storytelling, and visual brand execution. Reporting to the Vice President of Enrollment & Marketing, the Director develops and implements creative strategies that advance enrollment, strengthen institutional reputation, cultivate community engagement, and support donor and constituent relationships. The Director leads the College\u2019s social media presence; directs the development of video, photography, design, and multimedia content; manages creative workflow; and ensures that public-facing content reflects Crown\u2019s identity as a boldly Christian institution. The position supervises the Content Producer and assigned student workers and collaborates closely with internal stakeholders and external partners. Equipment Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, a personal computer and required software, cameras and multimedia-production equipment, printers, scanners, copy machines, and other equipment required by the position. Reports to Vice President of Enrollment & Marketing Essential Functions of the Job 25% CREATIVE MARKETING AND BRAND EXECUTION \u00b7 Develop and execute an integrated creative marketing strategy aligned with Crown College\u2019s mission, brand promise, strategic priorities, enrollment goals, and advancement objectives. \u00b7 Translate institutional and enrollment priorities into compelling creative concepts, campaigns, and audience-centered content. \u00b7 Provide creative direction for digital, social, print, video, photography, and multimedia projects. \u00b7 Ensure consistent application of Crown\u2019s brand standards, visual identity, tone, and Christian mission across channels and deliverables. \u00b7 Partner with the Director of Communications to align institutional messaging with creative execution and channel strategy. \u00b7 Advise the Vice President of Enrollment & Marketing on creative opportunities, emerging trends, audience engagement, and resource needs. 30% SOCIAL MEDIA \u00b7 Develop and execute a comprehensive organic social media strategy promoting Crown\u2019s brand, academic programs, student experience, events, outcomes, and strategic initiatives. \u00b7 Create, curate, edit, schedule, and publish engaging text, image, video, and multimedia content across Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, X, YouTube, and emerging platforms. \u00b7 Create, curate, and schedule content for the President\u2019s social media channels in coordination with appropriate institutional leaders. \u00b7 Develop and maintain a coordinated social media calendar that balances enrollment, institutional, advancement, athletics, academic, and community priorities. \u00b7 Provide active community management by monitoring and responding to comments, messages, mentions, and inquiries in a timely, professional, and mission-consistent manner. \u00b7 Monitor platform data, audience behavior, engagement, reach, traffic, and content performance using Sprout Social, native platform analytics, Google Analytics, and related tools; use findings to improve strategy and execution. \u00b7 Collaborate with the Social Media Leadership Committee and campus departments to maintain consistency, quality, coordination, and institutional standards. \u00b7 Establish procedures for account governance, access, moderation, archiving, escalation, and response to sensitive or emerging issues. \u00b7 Stay current on platform changes, algorithms, accessibility expectations, best practices, and emerging content formats. \u00b7 Train and equip student workers, interns, alumni, ambassadors, and campus contributors who participate in social media initiatives. 20% MULTIMEDIA STORYTELLING AND CONTENT PRODUCTION \u00b7 Lead the planning and production of video, photography, short-form content, interviews, campaign assets, and institutional storytelling. \u00b7 Supervise the Content Producer and provide clear briefs, priorities, timelines, feedback, and creative direction. \u00b7 Identify stories and visual opportunities that communicate Crown\u2019s mission, student experience, academic quality, community, and impact. \u00b7 Ensure multimedia content is technically strong, accessible, appropriately licensed, and prepared for effective use across platforms. \u00b7 Maintain an organized, searchable, and appropriately governed library of creative assets, releases, project files, and final deliverables. \u00b7 Balance event coverage with strategic enrollment, institutional storytelling, and campaign-production priorities. 15% CREATIVE SERVICES, CAMPAIGNS, AND CROSS-FUNCTIONAL COLLABORATION \u00b7 Manage creative intake, project briefs, prioritization, production calendars, review cycles, approvals, and delivery across multiple concurrent projects. \u00b7 Collaborate with Enrollment and Communications leaders to develop audience-focused campaigns, organic channel support, and recruitment materials. \u00b7 Execute print requests in collaboration with the content producer. \u00b7 Provide approved creative assets and content support to external marketing partners and collaborate to ensure timely, emotive, brand-aligned campaign execution. \u00b7 Partner with the Data team to review content and channel performance, support tracking requirements, and apply data-informed insights to creative testing and optimization. \u00b7 Coordinate with the President\u2019s Office, \u00a0Advancement, Athletics, Academics, Student Development, Operations and other areas to meet institutional priorities. \u00b7 Manage relationships with approved photographers, videographers, freelancers, vendors, and production partners as assigned. \u00b7 Ensure projects meet accessibility, copyright, licensing, privacy, release, and institutional policy requirements. 10% PERSONNEL LEADERSHIP, ADMINISTRATION, AND CONTINUOUS IMPROVEMENT \u00b7 Recruit, onboard, coach, supervise, and evaluate the Content Producer and assigned student workers. \u00b7 Establish team goals, work plans, production standards, service expectations, and professional-development priorities. \u00b7 Monitor relevant budgets, subscriptions, equipment, vendors, and production expenses within delegated authority. \u00b7 Develop and report appropriate creative and social media performance measures to the Vice President of Enrollment & Marketing. \u00b7 Maintain documentation, templates, calendars, account access, workflows, and continuity plans for critical creative-marketing functions. \u00b7 Participate in departmental and institutional meetings, planning, events, and professional development. \u00b7 Perform other duties as assigned. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities \u00b7 Strong desire to advance Christ-centered higher education through creative excellence and servant leadership. \u00b7 Advanced understanding of social media platforms, audience behavior, algorithms, content formats, community management, and channel best practices. \u00b7 Demonstrated ability to develop creative strategy and translate institutional goals into compelling, audience-centered content. \u00b7 Excellent written, visual, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. \u00b7 Proficiency with social media management and analytics tools such as Sprout Social, Meta Business Suite, YouTube Studio, Google Analytics, and comparable platforms. \u00b7 Proficiency with content-creation and creative-production tools such as Adobe Creative Cloud, Canva, video-editing software, photography tools, and related technologies. \u00b7 Strong understanding of photography, videography, editing, multimedia production, and digital asset management. \u00b7 Ability to interpret analytics, identify actionable insights, and optimize content based on audience and performance data. \u00b7 Strong creative judgment and the ability to protect and consistently apply institutional brand standards. \u00b7 Ability to supervise, coach, motivate, and develop professional employees and student workers. \u00b7 Excellent project-management, prioritization, organizational, and problem-solving skills in a fast-paced environment. \u00b7 Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, manage sensitive issues, and collaborate effectively across departments. \u00b7 Understanding of accessibility, copyright, licensing, permissions, privacy, and ethical content practices. \u00b7 High level of personal integrity, professionalism, initiative, adaptability, and attention to detail. \u00b7 Agreement with and commitment to the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant. Physical Demands The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to perform the essential functions of this position successfully. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. \u00b7 Sit or stand for extended periods and perform extensive computer and mobile-device work. \u00b7 Possess hand and arm dexterity, or an equivalent ability, sufficient for keyboard use and operation of creative-production equipment. \u00b7 Communicate effectively with coworkers, students, partners, and constituents by telephone, video conference, and in person. \u00b7 Possess adequate vision to accommodate frequent viewing of computer screens and review of visual content. \u00b7 Frequently lift or move up to 10 pounds and infrequently lift or move up to 25 pounds, including production equipment. \u00b7 Occasionally move throughout campus and off-campus locations and work in moderate-to-high noise environments during events. Minimum Qualifications \u00b7 Agreement with and commitment to abide by the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant. \u00b7 Bachelor\u2019s degree in marketing, communications, digital media, visual communications, public relations, or a related field. \u00b7 Five years of progressively responsible experience in creative marketing, social media, content strategy, digital communications, multimedia production, or a related area. \u00b7 Demonstrated experience developing and executing social media strategy, creating content, managing online communities, and using analytics to guide decisions. \u00b7 Demonstrated experience directing or producing video, photography, graphic, and multimedia content. \u00b7 Experience managing complex projects, production calendars, and cross-functional stakeholders. \u00b7 Supervisory experience or demonstrated experience leading employees, interns, students, vendors, or project teams. \u00b7 A portfolio demonstrating strong creative judgment and effective content across multiple platforms. Preferred Qualifications \u00b7 Master\u2019s degree in marketing, communications, digital media, business, higher education, or a related field. \u00b7 Seven or more years of progressively responsible experience in creative marketing or communications. \u00b7 Experience in higher education, nonprofit, ministry, or faith-based organizations. \u00b7 Experience leading creative services or content-production function. \u00b7 Experience supporting enrollment marketing, advancement, executive social media, or institutional reputation initiatives. \u00b7 Advanced experience with Adobe Creative Cloud, Sprout Social, Google Analytics, content-management systems, and digital asset-management tools. \u00b7 Crown College alumnus or familiarity with Crown College and The Christian and Missionary Alliance. Benefits Crown College offers a generous and comprehensive benefits package for full-time staff and faculty, designed to support the health, well-being, and financial future of our employees. Benefits include medical coverage through Medica, dental coverage through Delta Dental, and vision coverage through EyeMed. Employees also receive employer-paid basic life insurance equal to one times their annual salary, subject to policy limits, with optional voluntary benefits including supplemental life insurance, hospital indemnity, critical illness, and short-term disability coverage. A Health Savings Account (HSA) is available for employees enrolled in the high-deductible health plan. In addition to competitive benefits, Crown offers generous paid vacation, sick leave, and holiday pay, along with a 403(b) retirement plan that includes an employer contribution. Environment and Location Employees enjoy working on our beautiful lakeside campus, which features an on-campus fitness center, scenic walking paths leading to Parley Lake and convenient access to our on-campus Frisbie Golf Course. These amenities provide excellent opportunities to stay active, recharge, and enjoy the natural beauty of the campus throughout the year. Non-Discrimination Policy Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status regarding public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive.\u00a0 This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change.\u00a0 Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate all job duties as determined necessary.) Additional Information Base Pay From 55,000 Base Pay To 65,000 Base Pay Per Year"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=537208004": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type FTF Required Degree Masters Manage Others Yes Description This is a full time, tenure-track faculty position within the School of Health and Science teaching undergraduate nursing courses on campus and supervising nursing students in clinical settings. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Chair of the Department of Nursing. SUPERVISION RECEIVED This position reports to the Chair of the Department of Nursing, the Dean of the School of Health and Science, and the Vice President of Academic Affairs . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS Adjunct and clinical faculty who may be assigned within a course. EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION Works from an office at Crown College. Regular attendance on campus to complete job duties is required. Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and related software, printer, copy machines, Nursing Simulation Lab equipment and tools related to undergraduate teaching and research. Travel to clinical sites will also be required. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB \u00b7 Teach courses within the prescribed nursing curriculum utilizing a variety of teaching methodologies to engage students in the learning process. A normal teaching load is 24 credits each year. \u00b7 Teaching in simulation lab \u00b7 Facilitate student development of knowledge, skills, and demeanor required for professional practice as a nurse. \u00b7 Supervise students in clinical settings. \u00b7 Advise students in the Department of Nursing. \u00b7 Stay abreast of scholarly developments in specific and relevant fields as well as current teaching methodologies, curriculum development, and assessment. \u00b7 Contribute to the field of nursing and/or the profession of college-level teaching. \u00b7 Participate in measures to maintain compliance with Minnesota State Board of Nursing and Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education. \u00b7 Support the mission, goals and objectives of Crown College. \u00b7 Engage in general faculty responsibilities that include: o Participation in department and faculty meetings, o Care of students, o Crown College committee assignments, and o At least 10 hours of scheduled office hours on campus per week to be available to students. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES \u00b7 Demonstrated experience and expertise teaching nursing courses at the college level. \u00b7 Demonstrated experience in simulation labs. \u00b7 Strong interpersonal skills and an enthusiasm for working with students pursuing higher education. \u00b7 Established ability to work effectively as a team member. \u00b7 Demonstrate excellence and professionalism in spoken, written and electronic communication skills when with prospective and current students, faculty, and staff, as well as clinical agency representatives. \u00b7 Ability to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith. \u00b7 Experience evaluating students\u2019 work and reporting results promptly. \u00b7 Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant. \u00b7 Must be a committed Christian who is active in a local church PHYSICAL DEMANDS The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.\u00a0 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time (in the classroom, in the simulation lab, and in clinical settings). Mobility to allow for safe movement within lab and clinical environments. Hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to allow for patient care, safe use of equipment, and extensive use of a keyboard for data entry. Vocal strength to speak clearly in a classroom and lab for extended periods of time. Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials. Body strength to frequently lift and/ or move up to ten (10) pounds. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS \u00b7 Master of Science in Nursing or equivalent degree \u00b7 Relevant experience as a nurse \u00b7 Current unencumbered RN License \u00b7 Demonstrated teaching effectiveness \u00b7 Current American Heart Association Healthcare Provider BLS Certification (or equivalent). \u00b7 Experience using computer technology in the teaching/learning process PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications) \u00b7 Earned DNP, PhD in Nursing or other equivalent terminal degree. \u00b7 Experience as a nurse in OB, acute medical/surgical, ICU, Emergency, or related area. \u00b7 Unencumbered RN Licensure in Minnesota \u00b7 3+ years of full-time teaching experience, especially in Christian higher education \u00b7 Familiarity and/or experience with standards and assessments, especially related to the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education and the Minnesota Board of Nursing \u00b7 Experience with advising BENEFITS Crown College offers a generous and comprehensive benefits package for full-time staff and faculty, designed to support the health, well-being, and financial future of our employees. Benefits include medical coverage through Medica, dental coverage through Delta Dental, and vision coverage through EyeMed. Employees also receive employer-paid basic life insurance equal to one times their annual salary, subject to policy limits, with optional voluntary benefits including supplemental life insurance, hospital indemnity, critical illness, and short-term disability coverage. A Health Savings Account (HSA) is available for employees enrolled in the high-deductible health plan. In addition to competitive benefits, Crown offers generous paid vacation, sick leave, and holiday pay, along with a 403(b) retirement plan that includes an employer contribution. ENVIRONMENT AND LOCATION Employees enjoy working on our beautiful lakeside campus, which features an on-campus fitness center, scenic walking paths leading to Parley Lake and convenient access to our on-campus Frisbie Golf Course. These amenities provide excellent opportunities to stay active, recharge, and enjoy the natural beauty of the campus throughout the year. Non-Discrimination Policy Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status regarding public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive.\u00a0 This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change.\u00a0 Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate all job duties as determined necessary.) Additional Information Base Pay From $62,000 Base Pay To $73,000"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=537207621": {"title": "Current Crown College Student Position- Registrar Office Assistant", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Current Crown College Student Position- Registrar Office Assistant Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Student Contact information Name Hannah Goodall Email registrar@crown.edu Description Anticipated Start Date: 26 Aug 2026 Hours Worked Per Week: 10 hours per week during M-T-W-R-F, 8:00 AM \u2013 4:30 PM Job Definition - Registrar\u2019s Office student workers support staff by performing routine duties and assisting with projects related to student data management and academic records. Supervisor Name Hannah Goodall Supervisor Title Assistant Registrar Minimum Qualifications: Support and Model the policies and standards of Crown College as stated in the Student Handbook and Crown Community Covenant. Evidence of Christian character and a commitment to encourage others toward Christ-likeness. Maintain a 2.0 cumulative GPA. Must be in good standing with the college. Previous experience with administrative work preferred. Responsibilities - Maintain student electronic files and computer data with accuracy, efficiency, and confidentiality. Scan & link MDE forms FERPA Personal Information Updates Digitizing hard copy documents 30-day review Process student-related forms. Process internet submissions Student requests Name/address changes Transcript requests Transcript transfer entry Assist with the day-to-day operations of the office Courteous counter service Professional phone communication Email and print communications. Assist with editing Academic Catalog. Collaborate with Office of the Registrar staff in completing additional duties as needed. Data cleanup Research Graduation duties Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: High attention to detail and accuracy in completing tasks. Proficiency with basic computer applications, including email and word processing. Effective verbal and written communication skills. Interpersonal skills. Strong customer service orientation with a friendly and helpful demeanor. Maintain confidentiality regarding private student information. Demonstrated dependability and punctuality. Ability to manage time effectively and balance multiple responsibilities. Ability to understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Ability to work collaboratively and respectfully as part of a team. Strong problem-solving skills and ability to respond appropriately to unexpected situations. Professional demeanor, including appropriate appearance and conduct in the workplace. Physical Demands: Ability to lift and carry loads of up to 4 pounds. Ability to remain in a stationary position for extended periods while performing job duties. Additional Information Base Pay From 12.70 Base Pay Per Hour"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=520433365": {"title": "Faculty In Residence - Worship Ministry", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Faculty In Residence - Worship Ministry Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type FIR Required Degree Masters Manage Others Yes Description This is a part-time faculty position to teach undergraduate worship ministry courses on campus within the School of Arts and Sciences. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Chair of the Department of Biblical, Theological, and Ministry Studies. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: This position reports to the Chair of the Department of Biblical, Theological, and Ministry Studies, the Dean of the School of Liberal Arts, and the Vice President of Academic Affairs . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: Assigned students involved in chapel worship leadership and traveling worship teams EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION: Works from an office at Crown College.\u00a0 Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and required programs, printer, fax machine, calculator, copy machines, and other equipment as the position requires. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB: \u00b7 Teach two courses per normal academic term related to worship ministry. Courses may include \u00a0Technology in Worship, Performance and Practice in Worship Ministry, Worship Ministry Foundations and Practice, and/or supervision of student worship leaders. Additional topics and/or private music lessons may be available to qualified candidates. \u00b7 Hold an average of at least 6 office hours per week during the normal academic terms. \u00b7 Advise Worship Ministry students in the Department of Biblical, Theological, and Ministry Studies. \u00b7 Recruit new students to pursue BA in Worship Ministry or minor in Worship Ministry. \u00b7 Review related curricula and recommend modifications as appropriate \u00b7 Participate in department and faculty meetings as available \u00b7 Assist in securing adjunct instructors for worship classes and music instruction May also assist in mentoring and preparing worship leaders for on-campus Chapel worship and off-campus events by invitation REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: \u00b7 A Biblically-grounded and convictional theology of worship \u00b7 Demonstrated experience and expertise leading and teaching others to lead corporate worship \u00b7 Ability to perform vocally or instrumentally from standard musical notation, chord charts, and lead sheets \u00b7 Experience working with audio, video, and lighting equipment related to corporate worship \u00b7 Strong interpersonal skills and positive energy regarding professional education \u00b7 Established ability to work effectively as a team member \u00b7 Skill to organize and manage multiple tasks simultaneously \u00b7 Demonstrated excellence in spoken, written and electronic communication skills \u00b7 Ability to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith \u00b7 Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.\u00a0 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time in classroom and corporate worship environments Hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to allow for safe use of equipment and extensive use of a keyboard for data entry Vocal strength to speak clearly in classroom and worship contexts for extended periods of time Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials Body strength to frequently lift and/or move up to twenty-five (25) pounds MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: \u00b7 Bachelor\u2019s degree in worship, music, or related field and a Master\u2018s degree with at least 18 hours in the field(s) of worship/ministry leadership/music or the equivalent professional experience \u00b7 Significant experience leading corporate worship in an Evangelical church \u00b7 Experience using technology in teaching/learning processes, team organization, and tools related to corporate worship PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications): \u00b7 MDiv, ThD, PhD, or the equivalent from an Evangelical seminary or graduate school \u00b7 Ordination or Consecration in the Christian and Missionary Alliance \u00b7 Collegiate teaching experience \u00b7 Education and skills to teach private lessons in voice, piano, guitar and/or basic music classes NON-DISCRIMINATION POLICY: Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status with regard to public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive.\u00a0 This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change.\u00a0 Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate any and all job duties as necessary. Additional Information Base Pay From 15,000 Base Pay To 25,000"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=503706884": {"title": "On Campus Adjunct", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in On Campus Adjunct Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Adjunct - on campus Required Degree Masters Description EFFECTIVE DATE :\u00a0July 1, 2026 FLSA STATUS :\u00a0Exempt HOURS WORKED :\u00a09-18 hours weekly during regular academic terms This is an exempt, adjunct faculty position to teach undergraduate courses on campus. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Chair of the Department. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: This position reports to the Chair of the Department, the Dean of the School, and the Vice President of Academic Affairs. SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: None. EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION: Works from an office at Crown College.\u00a0 Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and required programs, printer, fax machine, calculator, copy machines, and other equipment as the position requires. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB: \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Teach courses according to specialty and needs of the college \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Stay abreast of scholarly developments in specific and relevant fields as well as current teaching methodologies, curriculum development, and assessment. \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Support the mission, goals and objectives of Crown College \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Engage in general faculty responsibilities that include but are not limited to care of students and scheduled office hours per week to be available to students REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Demonstrated experience and expertise teaching\u00a0 courses at the college level \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Strong interpersonal skills and positive energy regarding professional education \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Established ability to work effectively as a team member \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Demonstrate excellence in spoken, written and electronic communication skills \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Ability to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Experience evaluating students\u2019 work and reporting results promptly \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Must be a committed Christian who is active in a local church. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.\u00a0 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time in classroom Hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to allow for safe use of equipment and extensive use of a keyboard for data entry Vocal strength to speak clearly in classroom for extended periods of time Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials Body strength to frequently lift and/or move up to twenty-five (25) pounds MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Master\u2019s level degree \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Demonstrated teaching effectiveness \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Experience using computer technology in the teaching/learning process PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications): \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A PhD in related field \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a05+ years of full-time teaching experience, especially in Christian higher education \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a03+ years of full-time teaching K-12 in the field of history \u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Familiarity and/or experience with standards and assessments NON-DISCRIMINATION POLICY: Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status with regard to public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive.\u00a0 This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change.\u00a0 Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate any and all job duties as necessary.) Additional Information Base Pay From 800/ Load Hr Base Pay To 900/ Load Hr"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=503704519": {"title": "Mail Room Manager", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Mail Room Manager Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type FTS Required Degree High school Manage Others Yes Contact information Name Brian Schwarz Email schwarzb@crown.edu Description FLSA STATUS: Full-Time, Non-Exempt HOURS WORKED: Monday \u2013 Friday, daytime hours; limited, occasional evenings as needed. The Mail Room Manager is responsible for the day-to-day operation of Crown College\u2019s mail room, serving students, faculty, and staff. This includes receiving, securing, sorting, and distributing all incoming mail and packages; coordinating with the local U.S. Post Office, UPS, and FedEx; maintaining the student post office box system; processing outgoing mail; managing a small cash drawer; and notifying recipients when deliveries arrive. As mail room services transition in-house from Sodexo, the Mail Room Manager will help design, build, and continually improve the operation\u2014and then live in it day-to-day\u2014while engaging students in the relational, discipleship-minded culture of Christian higher education. SUPERVISION RECEIVED : The Mail Room Manager reports to the Executive Director of Operations. SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: The Mail Room Manager may supervise up to one student worker. EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION: Works from the campus mail room at Crown College. Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, a personal computer and required software programs, package-tracking and point-of-sale systems, postage and shipping equipment, package scanners, a cash drawer, hand trucks or carts, a printer, a copier, and other equipment as required by the position. Mail & Package Operations (40% of the job) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Liaise with the local U.S. Post Office, UPS, and FedEx to ensure all incoming packages are received, tracked, and properly secured \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Receive, log, and securely store all incoming mail and packages for students, faculty, and staff \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Sort incoming mail and deliver it to staff and faculty offices across campus \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Pick up outgoing mail from campus offices and prepare it for processing \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Drop off outgoing mail at the local post office as needed \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Notify students, faculty, and staff by email when packages and deliveries arrive for pickup \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Release packages only to the correct recipient and manage returns, forwarding, and undeliverable items Student Post Office Box System (20% of the job) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Maintain and manage the student post office box system, including box assignments, keys, and combinations \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Assign, reassign, and close out PO boxes each semester as students arrive and depart \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Keep accurate records linking students to their boxes and ensure the system stays current \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0File mail promptly and keep the PO box area orderly so students can reliably retrieve their mail Service Hours & Student Worker Coordination (15% of the job) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Maintain consistent, posted mail room hours so students can dependably pick up mail and packages \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Coordinate scheduling between self and up to one student worker to extend coverage and pickup hours \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Hire (in coordination with the Executive Director of Operations), train, schedule, and oversee the mail room student worker \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Provide a warm, service-oriented experience for every student and employee at the window Cash Handling & Vendor Relations (10% of the job) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Manage a small cash drawer for postage and mail drop-offs at the local post office \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Reconcile the cash drawer and maintain accurate records of mail-related expenditures in line with College financial policies \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Manage accounts and relationships with USPS, UPS, FedEx, and other shipping and postage vendors \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Monitor postage and shipping supplies and reorder as needed within budget System Build-Out & Transition (10% of the job) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Lead the in-house transition of mail room services from Sodexo, helping design and stand up the new operation \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Build practical workflows, signage, and procedures for receiving, logging, notifying, and distribution\u2014and refine them through daily use \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Identify and recommend tools or process improvements that make the mail room more efficient and student-friendly \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Document standard operating procedures so the system is sustainable and repeatable over time General Administrative (5% of the job) \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Respond to unknowns and urgent items that need an immediate response \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Engage students and the student worker in discipleship and mentorship consistent with Crown\u2019s mission \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Other duties as assigned by the Executive Director of Operations REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to track and secure a high volume of mail and packages \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0A friendly, service-oriented attitude and a genuine love for working with and serving college students \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0A self-driven, resourceful go-getter who can build and run a new operation with limited day-to-day oversight \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Willingness to be creative, build the system, and live in it \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Heart for Christian higher education and a desire to engage in discipleship and mentorship with students \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Ability to handle confidential information and follow privacy and mail-handling standards \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Basic proficiency with computers, email, and Microsoft Office, and comfort learning package-tracking and point-of-sale systems \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Reliable cash-handling and basic recordkeeping skills \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Well-developed communication skills, both written and oral PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described herein are representative of those required of an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Stand, walk, bend, and reach for extended periods while sorting and delivering mail. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Have hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to sort mail, operate equipment, and use a keyboard for data entry. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Talk and hear with enough proficiency to communicate with students, co-workers, and vendors by phone or in person. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Have adequate vision to read addresses and labels and to view computer screens. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Frequently lift and/or move up to 25 pounds and occasionally lift or move up to 50 pounds, and push or pull loaded mail carts. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0The noise level is usually moderate but may be loud. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0High school diploma or equivalent \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Valid driver\u2019s license and ability to become an approved Crown driver for post office runs \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Experience in customer service, mail and shipping, retail, or logistics PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications): \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Associate\u2019s or Bachelor\u2019s degree \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Prior mail room, shipping and receiving, or postal experience \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Experience working in a college or ministry setting \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Experience setting up or improving an operational process \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0A love for mail NON-DISCRIMINATION POLICY: Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status with regard to public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive. \u00a0This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change. \u00a0Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate any and all job duties as necessary. Additional Information Base Pay From 36,000 Base Pay To 50,000 Base Pay Per Year"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=486900101": {"title": "Adjunct - Professor of Nursing, On Campus", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Adjunct - Professor of Nursing, On Campus Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Adjunct - on campus Required Degree Masters Manage Others Yes Description EFFECTIVE DATE: August 1, 2026 FLSA STATUS: Exempt HOURS WORKED: TBD as course schedule and workload is determined This is an adjunct faculty position within the School of Health and Science, teaching undergraduate nursing courses on campus and/or supervising nursing students in clinical settings. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Department of Nursing Chair . SUPERVISION RECEIVED: This position reports to the Chair of the Department of Nursing, the Dean of the School of Health and Science, and the Vice President of Academic Affairs . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: Student Workers or Teaching Assistants as applicable EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION: Works from an office at Crown College. Regular attendance on campus or to a clinical site to complete job duties is required. Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and related software, printer, calculator, copy machines, Nursing Simulation Lab equipment and tools related to undergraduate teaching and research. Travel to clinical sites will also be required. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB: \u00b7 Teach courses within the prescribed nursing curriculum utilizing a variety of teaching methodologies to engage students in the learning process. \u00b7 Facilitate student development of knowledge, skills, and demeanor required for professional practice as a nurse. \u00b7 Supervise students in clinical settings if applicable to the teaching assignments. \u00b7 Stay abreast of scholarly developments in specific and relevant fields as well as current teaching methodologies, curriculum development, and assessment. \u00b7 Participate in measures to maintain compliance with Minnesota State Board of Nursing and Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education. \u00b7 Support the mission, goals and objectives of Crown College. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: \u00b7 Demonstrated experience and expertise in nursing with preference to experience teaching nursing courses at the college level \u00b7 Prefer demonstrated experience in simulation labs \u00b7 Strong interpersonal skills and positive energy regarding professional education \u00b7 Established ability to work effectively as a team member \u00b7 Demonstrate excellence and professionalism in spoken, written and electronic communication skills when with prospective and current students, faculty, and staff, as well as clinical agency representatives \u00b7 Ability to or willingness to learn how to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith \u00b7 Experience or willingness to learn how to evaluate students\u2019 work and report results promptly \u00b7 Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described herein are representative of those required of an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.\u00a0 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time (in the classroom, in the simulation lab, and in clinical settings). Mobility to allow for safe movement within lab and clinical environments. Hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to allow for patient care, safe use of equipment, and extensive use of a keyboard for data entry. Vocal strength to speak clearly in a classroom and lab for extended periods of time . Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials. Body strength to frequently lift and/ or move up to ten (10) pounds. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: \u00b7 Master of Science in Nursing or equivalent degree \u00b7 Relevant experience as a nurse \u00b7 Current unencumbered RN License \u00b7 Current American Heart Association Healthcare Provider BLS Certification (or equivalent). PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications): \u00b7 Earned DNP, PhD in Nursing or other equivalent terminal degree \u00b7 Experience as a nurse in acute medical/surgical, ICU, Emergency, or related area \u00b7 Unencumbered RN Licensure in Minnesota \u00b7 3+ years of full-time teaching experience, especially in Christian higher education \u00b7 Familiarity and/or experience with standards and assessments, especially related to the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education and the Minnesota Board of Nursing NON-DISCRIMINATION POLICY: Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status with regard to public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive.\u00a0 This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change.\u00a0 Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate any and all job duties as necessary. Additional Information Base Pay From 800/Load hr Base Pay To 900/ Load hr"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=486886168": {"title": "Faculty-in-Residence, Criminal Justice and Legal Studies", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Faculty-in-Residence, Criminal Justice and Legal Studies Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Required Degree Masters Manage Others No Contact information Name Dr. Chris Mathews Email mathewsc@crown.edu Description EFFECTIVE DATE: July 1, 2026 FLSA STATUS: Exempt HOURS WORKED: 15-20 hours weekly during regular academic terms This is a part-time faculty position to teach undergraduate criminal justice courses on campus within the School of Liberal Arts and Education. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Chair of the Department of Humanities and Social Science. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: This position reports to the Chair of the Department of Humanities and Social Science , the Dean of the School of Liberal Arts and Education , and the Vice President of Academic Affairs . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: None. EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION: Works from an office at Crown College.\u00a0 Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and required programs, printer, fax machine, calculator, copy machines, and other equipment as the position requires. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB: \u00b7 Teach two courses per normal academic term related to criminal justice. Courses may include Criminal Procedure, Criminal Statues & Enforcement, and Criminal Investigations. \u00b7 Hold an average of at least 6 office hours per week during the normal academic terms. Participate in department and faculty meetings as available Academic advising for Criminal Justice and Legal Studies students as needed REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES: \u00b7 Demonstrated experience and expertise in teaching criminal justice courses at the college level \u00b7 Strong interpersonal skills and positive energy regarding professional education \u00b7 Established ability to work effectively as a team member \u00b7 Demonstrate excellence in spoken, written and electronic communication skills \u00b7 Ability to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith \u00b7 Experience evaluating students\u2019 work and reporting results promptly \u00b7 Hands-on experience in the criminal justice or legal field through previous work and/or consulting experience \u00b7 Ability and willingness to stay abreast of the ever-changing criminal justice environment in order to maintain relevancy in teaching criminal justice courses to college-level students \u00b7 Skill to organize and manage multiple tasks simultaneously \u00b7 Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described herein are representative of those required of an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.\u00a0 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time in classroom Hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to allow for safe use of equipment and extensive use of a keyboard for data entry Vocal strength to speak clearly in classroom for extended periods of time Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials Body strength to frequently lift and/or move up to twenty-five (25) pounds MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: \u00b7 Master\u2019s level degree in criminal justice or a related field, or Bachelor degree in relevant criminal justice-related field AND a minimum of 10 years\u2019 direct experience in a relevant criminal justice-related field \u00b7 Demonstrated teaching effectiveness \u00b7 Work experience in criminal justice, law enforcement, law, corrections, or a related field \u00b7 Experience using computer technology in the teaching/learning process PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications): \u00b7 A PhD or terminal degree in a related field \u00b7 5+ years of full-time teaching experience, especially in Christian higher education \u00b7 Familiarity and/or experience with standards and assessments \u00b7 Experience with academic advising/mentoring NON-DISCRIMINATION POLICY: Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status with regard to public assistance. Additional Information Base Pay From 15,000 Base Pay To 25,000"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=486886164": {"title": "Current Crown College Student Position- Nursing Department Student Worker", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Current Crown College Student Position- Nursing Department Student Worker Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Student Manage Others No Contact information Name Liz Rodgers Phone rodgerse@crown.edu Description Anticipated Start Date: September 2, 2026. The nursing department is seeking a detail-oriented student worker to assist in preparations for nursing laboratory and simulation experiences. This position supports the nursing professor in preparing for in-person laboratory and clinical simulation experiences. Minimum Qualifications: Support and Model the policies and standards of Crown College as stated in the Student Handbook and Crown Community Covenant. Evidence of Christian character and a commitment to encourage others toward Christ-likeness. Maintain a 2.0 cumulative GPA. Must be in good standing with the college. Previous experience with administrative work preferred. Responsibilities - Provide a detailed list of tasks and responsibilities. Set up laboratory equipment in the nursing lab. Set up simulators, with the professor's help, for simulation experiences. Make copies of student materials for lab experiences. Support maintaining and cleaning the learning environment prior to and after the laboratory/simulation experience. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: High attention to detail and accuracy in completing tasks. Proficiency with basic computer applications, including email and word processing. Effective verbal and written communication skills. Interpersonal skills. Strong customer service orientation with a friendly and helpful demeanor. Ability to manage time effectively and balance multiple responsibilities. Ability to understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Ability to work collaboratively and respectfully as part of a team. Professional demeanor, including appropriate appearance and conduct in the workplace. Ability to follow safety and sanitation guidelines in all work areas. Physical ability to stand, walk, lift, and carry items up to 25 lbs. for extended periods. Physical Demands: Ability to move about campus and within work areas as required. Ability to lift and carry loads of up to 4 pounds. Ability to lift, carry, push, or pull items weighing up to 25 lbs. Ability to bend, stoop, reach, and perform repetitive motions as part of regular tasks. Ability to operate necessary equipment or tools safely in assigned work areas. Additional Information Base Pay From 12.70 Base Pay Per Hour"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=453355349": {"title": "Current Crown College Student Position- Student Receptionist", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Current Crown College Student Position- Student Receptionist Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Student Contact information Name Brandon Schmidly Email schmidlyb@crown.edu Description Hours Worked Per Week up to 15-20 hours The Crown College Student Receptionist will provide professional and courteous service via the telephone and in person to the members of the College community and the public. They will portray an image of Crown College that is consistent with its mission and lifestyle standards. Minimum Qualifications: Support and Model the policies and standards of Crown College as stated in the Student Handbook and Crown Community Covenant. Evidence of Christian character and a commitment to encourage others toward Christ-likeness. Must be in good standing with the college. Previous experience with administrative work preferred. Responsibilities - Provide a detailed list of tasks and responsibilities. \u2022 The student receptionist is immediately responsible to the Primary Receptionist \u2022 The student receptionist will promptly answer all calls and route them pleasantly and quickly \u2022 The student receptionist will assist visitors to the College, giving a pleasant greeting and offer of assistance. \u2022 The student receptionist will maintain familiarity with all current email and calendar information related to campus activity (guests, events, etc.) \u2022 The student receptionist will serve as the primary contact in the event of an emergency, assisting Student Development and Security personnel by conveying urgent information and contacting the appropriate emergency assistance \u2022 The student receptionist will process all incoming faxes electronically for college personnel and students \u2022 The student receptionist will issue temporary guest parking passes. \u2022 The student receptionist will maintain the professional appearance of the reception area by keeping it clean and free of unnecessary items \u2022 The student receptionist will maintain familiarity with the Receptionist Manual, attend all required meetings as scheduled, and fulfill all assigned shifts according to policy \u2022 The student receptionist will present a professional and appropriate personal appearance in keeping with scheduled campus events and according to the policy as listed in the Receptionist Manual \u2022 The student receptionist will perform various other tasks as requested by college personnel and as assigned by the Advancement Office. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: High attention to detail and accuracy in completing tasks. Proficiency with basic computer applications, including email and word processing. Effective verbal and written communication skills. Interpersonal skills. Strong customer service orientation with a friendly and helpful demeanor. Maintain confidentiality regarding private student information. Demonstrated dependability and punctuality. Ability to manage time effectively and balance multiple responsibilities. Ability to understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Ability to work collaboratively and respectfully as part of a team. Strong problem-solving skills and ability to respond appropriately to unexpected situations. Professional demeanor, including appropriate appearance and conduct in the workplace. Ability to follow safety and sanitation guidelines in all work areas. Physical Demands: Ability to remain in a stationary position for extended periods while performing job duties. Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Reliable, friendly, and professional \u2022 Extensive phone, office, and customer service experience Additional Information Base Pay From 12.70 Base Pay Per Hour"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=453337473": {"title": "Current Crown College Student Position- Content Creator (Campus Experience and Community Life)", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Current Crown College Student Position- Content Creator (Campus Experience and Community Life) Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Student Description The Student Content Creator will assist the Marketing Content Coordinator in providing content revolving around CAMPUS EXPERIENCE & COMMUNITY LIFE for social media channels in a variety of digital formats that accurately reflect Crown College. Minimum Qualifications: Support and Model the policies and standards of Crown College as stated in the Student Handbook and Crown Community Covenant. Evidence of Christian character and a commitment to encourage others toward Christ-likeness. Maintain a 2.0 cumulative GPA. Must be in good standing with the college. Responsibilities - Provide a detailed list of tasks and responsibilities. Campus Experience Coverage - Capture authentic student-life moments: studying, hanging out, serving, worshiping, and celebrating together. - Highlight Student Life and Residence Life events that showcase community and connection. - Represent a wide range of students, majors, and activities. Faith Discovery - Document chapel, worship, service projects, and ministry events that reflect spiritual growth. - Capture stories that show faith lived out authentically across campus. Community & Collaboration - Partner with Student Life and Campus Ministries to plan coverage. - Collaborate weekly with the Academic & Athletics creator to align storytelling and maintain visual consistency. Content Contribution - Upload photos and video clips to the shared folder weekly. - Suggest captions or short-form post ideas that align with Crown\u2019s \u201cLife + Faith\u201d storytelling wells. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: High attention to detail and accuracy in completing tasks., Proficiency with basic computer applications, including email and word processing., Effective verbal and written communication skills. Interpersonal skills. Ability to manage time effectively and balance multiple responsibilities., Ability to understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Ability to work collaboratively and respectfully as part of a team, Strong problem-solving skills and ability to respond appropriately to unexpected situations., Professional demeanor, including appropriate appearance and conduct in the workplace., Physical ability to stand, walk, lift, and carry items up to 25 lbs. for extended periods. Willingness to work a flexible schedule, including evenings or weekends as needed. Physical Demands: Ability to move about campus and within work areas as required., Ability to lift and carry loads of up to 4 pounds.? Ability to remain in a stationary position for extended periods while performing job duties. Physically able to fulfill duties. Ability to bend, stoop, reach, and perform repetitive motions as part of regular tasks., Ability to operate necessary equipment or tools safely in assigned work areas. Preferred Qualifications: - Experience with Canva, Lightroom, or mobile editing apps (CapCut, Adobe Rush, VSCO) - Prior experience in photography, social media, or creative roles - Involvement in athletics, Student Life, or creative arts at Crown Additional Information Base Pay From 12.70 Base Pay Per Hour"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=436588295": {"title": "Current Crown College Student Position-Student Food Service Worker", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Current Crown College Student Position-Student Food Service Worker Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Student - Sodexo Contact information Name Stan Hadiwibowo Email stanley.hadiwibowo@sodexo.com Description Anticipated Start Date 28 Aug 2025 Hours Worked Per Week 10-15 Job Definition - This is a short and brief summary. (Example: The Student Development Assistant provides support to the Student Development Division.) Supporting Food Services operations in various capacity in various outlets within Crown College Supervisor Name Stan Hadiwibowo Supervisor Title General Manager Minimum Qualifications: Support and Model the policies and standards of Crown College as stated in the Student Handbook and Crown Community Covenant. Responsibilities - Provide a detailed list of tasks and responsibilities. \u2022Washes dishes by hand or places them in a dishwashing machine. \u2022Washes worktables, walls, and other surfaces. \u2022Sweeps, mops, cleans and vacuums floors. \u2022Removes trash and garbage to designated areas. \u2022Transfers supplies and equipment within and between storage and work areas such as pantry and dish room. \u2022Cleans equipment using specific chemicals to ensure sanitary standards. \u2022Polishes silver. \u2022May wash pots and pans. \u2022Attends all allergy and foodborne illness in-service training. \u2022Complies with all Sodexo HACCP policies and procedures. \u2022Reports all accidents and injuries in a timely manner. \u2022Complies with all company safety and risk management policies and procedures. \u2022May perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: High attention to detail and accuracy in completing tasks. Strong customer service orientation with a friendly and helpful demeanor. Demonstrated dependability and punctuality. Ability to manage time effectively and balance multiple responsibilities. Ability to understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Ability to work collaboratively and respectfully as part of a team. Strong problem-solving skills and ability to respond appropriately to unexpected situations. Professional demeanor, including appropriate appearance and conduct in the workplace. Ability to follow safety and sanitation guidelines in all work areas. Physical ability to stand, walk, lift, and carry items up to 25 lbs. for extended periods. Knowledge of proper food handling or basic cleaning procedures. Willingness to work a flexible schedule, including evenings or weekends as needed. Physical Demands: Ability to lift and carry loads of up to 4 pounds.? ,Physically able to fulfill duties. ,Ability to lift, carry, push, or pull items weighing up to 25 lbs., Ability to bend, stoop, reach, and perform repetitive motions as part of regular tasks. Ability to operate necessary equipment or tools safely in assigned work areas. Preferred Qualifications: Some Food Service experience Additional Information Base Pay From 12.70 Base Pay To 15 Base Pay Per Hour"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=436588293": {"title": "Current Crown College Student Position - Athletics Student Worker", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Current Crown College Student Position - Athletics Student Worker Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Student Contact information Name Jacob Van Dam Email vandamj@crown.edu Description Anticipated Start Date 28 Aug 2025 Hours Worked Per Week 5-15 Game Day Operations Student Workers play a vital role in ensuring the smooth execution of athletic events. Responsibilities include setting up and tearing down events, livestreaming, scoring tables, concessions, ticketing, facility upkeep, ball runners, chain gangs, and live stats. Evening and weekend availability is required. Supervisor Name Jacob Van Dam Supervisor Title Assistant Athletic Director for Communications and Operations Minimum Qualifications: Support and Model the policies and standards of Crown College as stated in the Student Handbook and Crown Community Covenant. ,Maintain a 2.0 cumulative GPA. Responsibilities - Provide a detailed list of tasks and responsibilities. Potential tasks and responsibilities include: Livestream Broadcast Live Stats Scoreboard Game Clock Concessions Ticketing Chain gang Ball Runners Photography Facility Upkeep Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong customer service orientation with a friendly and helpful demeanor., Demonstrated dependability and punctuality., Ability to manage time effectively and balance multiple responsibilities., Ability to understand and follow written and verbal instructions., Ability to work collaboratively and respectfully as part of a team., Professional demeanor, including appropriate appearance and conduct in the workplace., Physical ability to stand, walk, lift, and carry items up to 25 lbs. for extended periods. Willingness to work a flexible schedule, including evenings or weekends as needed. Physical Demands: Ability to move about campus and within work areas as required., Ability to lift and carry loads of up to 4 pounds.? ,Ability to remain in a stationary position for extended periods while performing job duties. Physically able to fulfill duties. ,Ability to bend, stoop, reach, and perform repetitive motions as part of regular tasks. Additional Information Base Pay From 12.70 Base Pay Per Hour"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=436585488": {"title": "Adjunct Professor of Biology", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Adjunct Professor of Biology Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Adjunct - on campus Required Degree Masters Contact information Name Krista Hoekstra Email hoekstrak@crown.edu Description This is an exempt, adjunct faculty position to teach undergraduate courses on campus within the School of Health and Science. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Chair of Biological and Health Sciences. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: This position reports to the Chair of Biological and Health Sciences, the Dean of the School of Health and Science, and the Vice President of Academic Affairs . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: Student Workers or Teaching Assistants as applicable EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION: Works from an office at Crown College. Regular attendance on campus to complete job duties is required. Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and related software, printer, copy machines, science lab equipment and tools related to undergraduate teaching and research. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB: \u00b7 Teach courses in, but not limited to, Biology, Ecology, Botany and Zoology. \u00b7 Prepare, administer and clean-up required labs and related equipment each week and participate in the overall maintenance of the science labs. \u00b7 Facilitate student development of knowledge, skills, and demeanor required to support the degrees which include Biology and Medical Biology/Health Sciences. \u00b7 Support the mission, goals and objectives of Crown College \u00b7 Engage in general faculty responsibilities that include but are not limited to: care of students and scheduled office hours per week to be available to students REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: \u00b7 Demonstrated experience and expertise teaching Biology courses at the college level. \u00b7 Strong interpersonal skills and positive energy regarding professional education. \u00b7 Established ability to work effectively as a team member. \u00b7 Demonstrate excellence in spoken, written and electronic communication skills. \u00b7 Ability to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith. \u00b7 Experience evaluating students\u2019 work and reporting results promptly. \u00b7 Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant. \u00b7 Must be a committed Christian who is active in a local church. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.\u00a0 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time (i.e. in the classroom). Mobility to allow for safe movement within campus and classroom environments. Vocal strength to speak clearly in a classroom for extended periods of time . Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials. Body strength to frequently lift and/ or move up to ten (10) pounds. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: \u00b7 Master of Science degree in Biology or related field \u00b7 Demonstrated teaching effectiveness \u00b7 Experience using computer technology in the teaching/learning process \u00b7 Demonstrated curriculum designing PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications): \u00b7 Earned PhD in Biology or related field. \u00b7 5+ years of full-time teaching experience, especially in Christian higher education \u00b7 3+ years of full-time teaching K-12 in the field of science \u00b7 Familiarity and/or experience with standards and assessments NON-DISCRIMINATION POLICY: Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status with regard to public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive.\u00a0 This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change.\u00a0 Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate any and all job duties as necessary.)"}, "https://secure5.entertimeonline.com/ta/CBIZ20706.careers?ShowJob=436585487": {"title": "Adjunct Professor of Math", "description": "CBIZ20706:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Adjunct Professor of Math Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 8700 College View Drive,\n    \n                      Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375,\n                      United States Employee Type Adjunct - on campus Required Degree Masters Contact information Name Krista Hoekstra Email hoekstrak@crown.edu Description This is an exempt, adjunct faculty position to teach undergraduate courses on campus within the School of Health and Science. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Chair of Biological and Health Sciences. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: This position reports to the Chair of Biological and Health Sciences, the Dean of the School of Health and Science, and the Vice President of Academic Affairs . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: Student Workers or Teaching Assistants as applicable EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION: Works from an office at Crown College. Regular attendance on campus to complete job duties is required. Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and related software, printer, copy machines, science lab equipment and tools related to undergraduate teaching and research. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB: \u00b7 Teach courses in, but not limited to, Math. \u00b7 Facilitate student development of knowledge, skills, and demeanor required to support the degrees which include Biology and Medical Biology/Health Sciences. \u00b7 Support the mission, goals and objectives of Crown College \u00b7 Engage in general faculty responsibilities that include but are not limited to: care of students and scheduled office hours per week to be available to students REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: \u00b7 Demonstrated experience and expertise teaching Math courses at the college level. \u00b7 Strong interpersonal skills and positive energy regarding professional education. \u00b7 Established ability to work effectively as a team member. \u00b7 Demonstrate excellence in spoken, written and electronic communication skills. \u00b7 Ability to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith. \u00b7 Experience evaluating students\u2019 work and reporting results promptly. \u00b7 Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant. \u00b7 Must be a committed Christian who is active in a local church. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.\u00a0 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time (i.e. in the classroom). Mobility to allow for safe movement within campus and classroom environments. Vocal strength to speak clearly in a classroom for extended periods of time . Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials. Body strength to frequently lift and/ or move up to ten (10) pounds. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: \u00b7 Master of Science degree in Math or related field \u00b7 Demonstrated teaching effectiveness \u00b7 Experience using computer technology in the teaching/learning process \u00b7 Demonstrated curriculum designing PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications): \u00b7 Earned PhD in Math or related field. \u00b7 5+ years of full-time teaching experience, especially in Christian higher education \u00b7 3+ years of full-time teaching K-12 in the field of science \u00b7 Familiarity and/or experience with standards and assessments NON-DISCRIMINATION POLICY: Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status with regard to public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and